{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_kuiajkluh3vpv37stuivzy6xyuzzyhco7ey6qylr3ba4ntfy27ia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass, and the Rust translation required **no behavioural fixes** — it was already byte-identical to the C.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- [x] **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` diff between the two `.so`s is **empty** (all 6: `create_state`, `destroy_state`, `process_buffer`, `update_flags`, `confuse_types`, `confusion`). 0 non-libc undefined symbols; `ldd -r` clean. Asserted programmatically by `phase_d_symbols.rs`.\n- [x] **Phase B** — all **34 `CONFIGS.md` rows** pass across fixed-seed randomized inputs, plus a 20,000-case soak.\n- [x] **Phase C** — all **26 `ERRORS.md` rows** have passing differential tests, plus 4 generic-boundary tests (null pointers, zero/oversized lengths, out-of-range \"enum\" sweep `-600..600` + `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`).\n- [x] **All 6 configurations** pass (`{default, --no-default-features, --all-features}` × `{dev, release}`) — 74 tests each.\n\n## What's compared per call\n\nReturn values, the full `ProcessState` (including the otherwise-invisible `status`/`reserved` bit-fields), **byte-exact stdout** (fd 1 captured around every call), and **allocator traces** (`malloc`/`free` counts + bytes via an `LD_PRELOAD` shim — 2/2/152, no leaks).\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not build a `cdylib`.** My first run silently fell back to a stale `target/release` object. I made path resolution strict (no cross-profile fallback) and each configuration now runs `cargo build` first — otherwise release runs would have been testing the wrong artifact.\n\n2. **fd 1 is process-wide**, so parallel tests corrupted captures with libtest's own progress output. Fixed via `.cargo/config.toml` (`RUST_TEST_THREADS = 1`) *and* a hard assertion, so a parallel run fails loudly instead of comparing garbage.\n\n## Anti-vacuity evidence\n\nRather than only reporting green, I injected 10 realistic bugs (`check-suite-detects-bugs.sh`) — saturating float cast, wrong bit-field offset, `& 0x7F` vs `& 0xFF`, unsigned byte sum, `memchr` off-by-one, zero- vs sign-extended `capacity`, altered format string, wrong `switch` default. **All 10 were caught.** `harness_selfcheck.rs` also proves the driver fails on divergence and that captures are non-empty.\n\nRows I could not reach honestly are handled rather than hand-waved: **E1/E3/E23** (allocation failure) are driven *for real* with an `LD_PRELOAD` shim failing one `malloc` of a chosen size in a child process; **E26** (signed overflow in `confusion`) is proved unreachable by a bound argument — the `f32` grid caps `confuse_types` at `INT_MAX - 127` while the other addends total ≤ 126 — so the test drives both reachable extremes instead.\n\n`c_src/` is untouched (original mtimes intact); only `c_src/build/` was created, as instructed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":432,"cache_read_input_tokens":199672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":432,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75bed887-5dcd-40a7-9a5d-1ad5587ae885","uuid":"72f9127d-53c9-4e45-9ada-060504b19c51","timestamp":"2026-08-28T00:19:38.016Z"}
